  "id": "COMPOUND:22069 - PROTEIN:5783",
  "verbalization": "Cocosamide B is implicated in the biological pathway leading to M19-MEL through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Cocosamide B acts as a target for multiple entities, including MOVP-3, SNB-78, and Hepatocyte, which are all targets of the same compound, 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. This compound is consistently identified as a key mediator in the pathway connecting Cocosamide B to M19-MEL, with each step in the chain reinforcing the relationship. The shared target of 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One across different targets of Cocosamide B suggests a potential mechanism of action involving this compound. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One as a central mediator in the signaling cascade initiated by Cocosamide B, ultimately leading to the interaction with M19-MEL.",
